1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:16,480
And so, having completed their promised kiss, the two began a journey beyond Severance, guided by the Star of Love.

2
00:00:18,240 --> 00:00:21,700
Hey, Mommy, what's your new book going to be about?

3
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:29,000
It's the story of you and your friend, the girl who taught us all about Kumaria. This is the last page.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,080
Huh? I don't know what girl you mean.

5
00:00:33,560 --> 00:00:40,240
Of course you know what girl. She's the one you love. Don't you remember telling me you sang the love song together?

6
00:00:41,520 --> 00:00:43,840
I don't know any girl like that.

7
00:00:43,840 --> 00:00:49,880
What? Oh, Kureha, what's happened? Don't tell me you've forgotten her.

8
00:00:49,880 --> 00:01:04,200
From the beginning, we hated you. But also, we loved you from the beginning as well.

9
00:01:04,200 --> 00:01:10,200
All we wanted was to become true friends with you. So we had to cross the wall.

10
00:01:10,200 --> 00:01:13,880
You're in Kuma!

11
00:01:13,880 --> 00:01:19,580
You're in Kuma Harashi!

12
00:02:51,046 --> 00:03:07,266
It was amazing. I wish she could have seen the look on Kureha's face.

13
00:03:09,006 --> 00:03:11,186
I didn't expect it to feel so good.

14
00:03:11,866 --> 00:03:13,746
Thank you for choosing me from the crowd.

15
00:03:14,526 --> 00:03:16,066
You found me, and I love you.

16
00:03:16,526 --> 00:03:20,746
I'm not a weak girl at the mercy of the invisible storm anymore.

17
00:03:22,046 --> 00:03:26,366
I'm far too important, and we'll never get excluded now. It's wonderful.

18
00:03:28,546 --> 00:03:29,346
Chuck!

19
00:03:38,346 --> 00:03:43,746
Simmer, simmer, porridge, simmer, simmer, softly. Growl, growl, growl.

20
00:03:44,466 --> 00:03:48,946
After Ginkgo saved her letter, Curry Pie gave us official permission to freeload at her house.

21
00:03:48,946 --> 00:03:51,626
We're so close now, Lulu can almost taste it.

22
00:03:52,626 --> 00:03:57,646
Ginkgo's gone through a lot, but it seems like it's just a matter of time before she gets her promised kiss.

23
00:03:57,646 --> 00:04:11,066
It won't! I'll never back down on love!

24
00:04:11,066 --> 00:04:19,266
I don't understand. Why would you protect Sumika's letter for me?

25
00:04:20,346 --> 00:04:22,446
Why, when it cost you so much?

26
00:04:22,446 --> 00:04:34,106
Ginkgo, oh good. I'm glad you're awake.

27
00:04:34,106 --> 00:04:43,746
If you want, I can tell you all about my love.

28
00:04:44,386 --> 00:04:44,786
Oh.

29
00:04:44,786 --> 00:04:52,126
As long as you don't forget, love, you'll never, ever be truly alone.

30
00:04:52,346 --> 00:04:56,366
And if you don't give up on love, even if you lose something, you'll never be invisible.

31
00:04:56,926 --> 00:04:58,726
Wait, how do you know those words?

32
00:04:59,246 --> 00:05:01,746
You are and have always been my Lady Kumaria.

33
00:05:03,026 --> 00:05:04,346
Your Lady Kumaria?

34
00:05:05,066 --> 00:05:07,466
Like the one from Mom's book?

35
00:05:07,466 --> 00:05:22,546
Delicious smell. You smell, Kareha.

36
00:05:23,026 --> 00:05:23,726
Growl, growl.

37
00:05:24,626 --> 00:05:28,066
You need to search. You need to find what you want.

38
00:05:28,226 --> 00:05:30,106
But does what I want need to be found?

39
00:05:30,346 --> 00:05:30,826
Yes.

40
00:05:32,406 --> 00:05:36,446
I don't know what to look for, and I don't know where to find it.

41
00:05:36,446 --> 00:05:40,686
I know you remember. It's in your fingers, in your lips.

42
00:05:41,506 --> 00:05:44,026
It's inside you, right here.

43
00:05:45,306 --> 00:05:48,226
Please, will you give me the promise kiss?

44
00:05:48,366 --> 00:05:52,306
Promise kiss? From me to you?

45
00:05:52,306 --> 00:05:53,686
And me to you.

46
00:05:54,206 --> 00:05:57,866
Then everything will awaken, and it will all change.

47
00:05:57,866 --> 00:06:07,786
Whoa. What was that?

48
00:06:13,786 --> 00:06:16,466
Oh, wow. What a thing to dream.

49
00:06:17,466 --> 00:06:19,966
Growl. The honey porridge is ready.

50
00:06:19,966 --> 00:06:28,106
Is everything all right?

51
00:06:28,326 --> 00:06:29,646
You're blushing, curry pie.

52
00:06:33,386 --> 00:06:34,586
Just your imagination.

53
00:06:35,206 --> 00:06:37,366
You don't mind keeping your eye on Ginkgo, do you?

54
00:06:37,586 --> 00:06:38,666
She's sweating a lot.

55
00:06:39,026 --> 00:06:39,386
Thanks.

56
00:06:42,026 --> 00:06:42,626
Growl.

57
00:06:42,626 --> 00:06:47,806
My lady, Kumari.

58
00:06:51,806 --> 00:06:53,766
What would I dream that for?

59
00:06:54,706 --> 00:06:57,686
Kareha, did you have fun with your friend again today?

60
00:06:58,126 --> 00:06:59,806
Yep. Guess what, Mom?

61
00:06:59,966 --> 00:07:01,966
I taught her how to sing the love song.

62
00:07:01,966 --> 00:07:04,426
Oh, my. You did?

63
00:07:05,246 --> 00:07:08,086
Uh-huh. It's because she's my special friend.

64
00:07:08,366 --> 00:07:10,206
So I figured she gets an exception.

65
00:07:10,606 --> 00:07:13,926
I see. You really love her, don't you, sweetie?

66
00:07:14,986 --> 00:07:16,606
Yeah, I do.

67
00:07:19,606 --> 00:07:21,926
Her? Who is her?

68
00:07:21,926 --> 00:07:22,886
Maybe...

69
00:07:22,886 --> 00:07:27,546
How could I forget?

70
00:07:28,546 --> 00:07:30,086
I did have a friend.

71
00:07:31,086 --> 00:07:32,486
Mom, please help me.

72
00:07:33,446 --> 00:07:34,806
Who was that girl?

73
00:07:35,726 --> 00:07:37,866
I think I'm starting to remember.

74
00:07:44,566 --> 00:07:46,706
I heard there was another bear attack.

75
00:07:46,926 --> 00:07:49,406
No way. Wasn't it exterminated, though?

76
00:07:49,686 --> 00:07:51,566
I thought that girl shot it.

77
00:07:51,926 --> 00:07:52,746
You know, what's her name?

78
00:07:52,926 --> 00:07:53,366
Oh, yeah.

79
00:07:53,586 --> 00:07:55,786
The one who attracts bad luck to, like, everyone.

80
00:07:56,186 --> 00:07:57,306
Whether she did or not,

81
00:07:57,526 --> 00:08:00,546
I'm telling you, another girl from her class totally got attacked.

82
00:08:00,746 --> 00:08:01,346
For real?

83
00:08:01,526 --> 00:08:02,266
For real.

84
00:08:02,866 --> 00:08:04,626
So, who was it this time?

85
00:08:05,846 --> 00:08:06,266
What?

86
00:08:06,806 --> 00:08:07,886
Kaoru Harishima?

87
00:08:13,486 --> 00:08:16,506
Yes, she was discovered this morning in front of the flower bed.

88
00:08:16,506 --> 00:08:20,066
They declared it a bear attack based on the poor girl's injuries.

89
00:08:20,406 --> 00:08:21,086
But how?

90
00:08:21,086 --> 00:08:23,006
Oh, I thought I shot that bear.

91
00:08:23,206 --> 00:08:27,226
Which means, unfortunately, there's yet another bear still roaming the halls of this school.

92
00:08:27,606 --> 00:08:28,406
It's horrifying.

93
00:08:29,126 --> 00:08:30,966
The bears didn't just take Rea's life.

94
00:08:31,366 --> 00:08:33,046
They stole the proof of our love.

95
00:08:33,906 --> 00:08:35,966
They took the star pendant I gave her.

96
00:08:37,646 --> 00:08:38,666
Oh, Miss Yuriyika.

97
00:08:39,426 --> 00:08:41,106
The bear with Rea's pendant.

98
00:08:41,746 --> 00:08:43,366
That one is our mortal enemy.

99
00:08:44,326 --> 00:08:45,566
One day we'll find it.

100
00:08:45,566 --> 00:08:46,486
And then...

101
00:08:46,486 --> 00:08:50,486
And then I'll kill it.

102
00:08:50,486 --> 00:08:53,666
I'm so sorry.

103
00:08:53,946 --> 00:08:56,306
You came here to ask me about something, didn't you, dear?

104
00:08:56,746 --> 00:08:57,186
Yes.

105
00:08:57,366 --> 00:08:58,586
It's about an old friend.

106
00:08:58,946 --> 00:09:00,326
I'd like to know what you know.

107
00:09:00,446 --> 00:09:01,986
An old friend of yours?

108
00:09:02,186 --> 00:09:02,506
Right.

109
00:09:02,506 --> 00:09:05,766
I remembered her while I was listening to Mom's music box.

110
00:09:06,426 --> 00:09:10,186
When I was younger, apparently I had a friend who was very special to me.

111
00:09:10,766 --> 00:09:12,166
I know this girl is her.

112
00:09:12,846 --> 00:09:16,426
But for some weird reason, I can't remember her face or her real name.

113
00:09:16,426 --> 00:09:19,826
I was hoping you might know something more about my friend.

114
00:09:22,606 --> 00:09:26,226
Come to think of it, Rea made a rather strange comment once.

115
00:09:26,406 --> 00:09:28,286
It was shortly before she died, I think.

116
00:09:29,126 --> 00:09:33,226
She told me you had suddenly and completely forgotten about a close friend.

117
00:09:33,926 --> 00:09:34,246
Huh?

118
00:09:34,826 --> 00:09:35,666
What else?

119
00:09:36,266 --> 00:09:37,766
Ah, yes, her last book.

120
00:09:38,086 --> 00:09:39,606
The Moon Girl and the Forest Girl.

121
00:09:40,186 --> 00:09:43,206
She said she wrote that story about you and that forgotten girl.

122
00:09:43,206 --> 00:09:48,266
Mom's last book was about me and my friend?

123
00:09:49,666 --> 00:09:51,506
Ginkgo, hang in there.

124
00:09:52,766 --> 00:09:56,006
Sniffle-grow, your fever's not going down.

125
00:09:58,146 --> 00:09:59,346
Lulu knows.

126
00:10:02,266 --> 00:10:06,446
This will turn you into a nice cold growl-sicle and you'll feel way better.

127
00:10:07,706 --> 00:10:09,086
Lulu is so clever.

128
00:10:13,206 --> 00:10:20,186
Kumariya is love.

129
00:10:20,786 --> 00:10:26,006
As the world's mother, she is the one who approves all living things and gives them love.

130
00:10:31,886 --> 00:10:36,666
The cub who appeared the day of that silvery blizzard was named Ginkgo.

131
00:10:36,666 --> 00:10:46,646
You're an unwanted bear, you know.

132
00:10:46,906 --> 00:10:50,046
A lonely lone wolf's bane that'll never be wanted by anybody.

133
00:10:51,186 --> 00:10:52,806
Hey, what's this about?

134
00:10:53,006 --> 00:10:55,106
What, you think you're the lone wolf's bane princess?

135
00:10:56,886 --> 00:10:58,206
Lone wolf's bane.

136
00:10:59,586 --> 00:11:01,126
Lone wolf's bane.

137
00:11:02,086 --> 00:11:03,566
Lone wolf's bane.

138
00:11:03,566 --> 00:11:06,326
Kurosuke!

139
00:11:07,006 --> 00:11:08,426
Shut up!

140
00:11:10,586 --> 00:11:13,466
And so Ginkgo was left all alone.

141
00:11:13,906 --> 00:11:17,926
For obvious reasons, she became known as Ginkgo the Lone Wolf's Bane.

142
00:11:18,346 --> 00:11:19,886
I understand now.

143
00:11:20,386 --> 00:11:22,406
This world is ruled by power.

144
00:11:23,406 --> 00:11:26,006
No one will ever be kind to the weak ones.

145
00:11:26,506 --> 00:11:29,046
It's a dog-eat-dog world and bear-eat-salmon.

146
00:11:30,006 --> 00:11:31,746
Kumami, dinner time!

147
00:11:31,746 --> 00:11:32,506
Okay!

148
00:11:34,086 --> 00:11:36,286
Kumako, come back home!

149
00:11:36,846 --> 00:11:37,506
Okay!

150
00:11:38,766 --> 00:11:39,566
Kumari!

151
00:11:39,866 --> 00:11:40,206
Okay!

152
00:11:40,746 --> 00:11:41,646
Kumagaret!

153
00:11:41,886 --> 00:11:42,346
Okay!

154
00:11:42,406 --> 00:11:42,846
Kumakaron!

155
00:11:43,186 --> 00:11:43,526
Okay!

156
00:11:45,606 --> 00:11:47,606
Kumakaron, today's your favorite!

157
00:11:47,986 --> 00:11:48,726
Salmon pizza!

158
00:11:49,166 --> 00:11:49,706
Hooray!

159
00:11:49,806 --> 00:11:51,286
I love salmon pizza!

160
00:11:53,186 --> 00:11:55,486
You are just so adorable!

161
00:11:55,486 --> 00:12:00,106
Eventually, the day of severance came.

162
00:12:05,826 --> 00:12:10,826
Bear cubs and Ginkgo's situation were gathered up by the superior, Lady Coomaster.

163
00:12:10,826 --> 00:12:17,926
Rejoice, my children, for you have finally been found.

164
00:12:18,526 --> 00:12:23,126
Yes, surely you are unwanted bears, but now you shall be given a chance at approval.

165
00:12:25,166 --> 00:12:29,106
In this world, only one needs you and gives you approval.

166
00:12:29,106 --> 00:12:32,086
We thank her daily for her love and graciousness.

167
00:12:32,386 --> 00:12:34,246
Thank you, Lady Kumaria!

168
00:12:34,746 --> 00:12:35,866
Lady Kumaria?

169
00:12:36,746 --> 00:12:40,666
From this day forth, you are cubs of Kumaria.

170
00:12:41,126 --> 00:12:46,906
You shall be guard bears and defend the great boundary between bear and human.

171
00:12:46,906 --> 00:12:54,866
Exclude the vermin known as humans from our border and eliminate them in order to protect

172
00:12:54,866 --> 00:12:55,706
our world.

173
00:12:56,086 --> 00:13:01,606
That is the mission you shall carry out for us, for we are the ones loved by Holy Mother

174
00:13:01,606 --> 00:13:02,366
Glomaria!

175
00:13:10,366 --> 00:13:11,366
Growl!

176
00:13:11,686 --> 00:13:12,026
Ah!

177
00:13:12,966 --> 00:13:14,266
Human excluded!

178
00:13:14,466 --> 00:13:15,266
Growl, growl!

179
00:13:15,266 --> 00:13:18,286
Growl!

180
00:13:19,666 --> 00:13:20,326
Ah!

181
00:13:20,906 --> 00:13:22,226
Human excluded!

182
00:13:22,526 --> 00:13:23,406
Growl, growl!

183
00:13:25,886 --> 00:13:26,806
Growl!

184
00:13:28,566 --> 00:13:30,126
Human excluded!

185
00:13:30,526 --> 00:13:31,426
Growl, growl!

186
00:13:32,046 --> 00:13:34,986
HQ, HQ, request backup immediately!

187
00:13:34,986 --> 00:13:36,986
Oh, please!

188
00:13:44,986 --> 00:13:46,986
Mary McClurdy!

189
00:13:53,986 --> 00:13:56,986
Ginkgo believed if she fulfilled her mission,

190
00:13:56,986 --> 00:13:59,986
surely Kumaria would approve of her

191
00:13:59,986 --> 00:14:02,986
and she would one day be granted love.

192
00:14:02,986 --> 00:14:05,986
I'm not an unwanted lone wolfsbane.

193
00:14:05,986 --> 00:14:07,986
I'll keep eating more and more people

194
00:14:07,986 --> 00:14:09,986
and someday I'll get approved.

195
00:14:09,986 --> 00:14:13,986
Soon enough, Lady Kumaria will do it.

196
00:14:21,986 --> 00:14:24,986
I'll finally be granted my love.

197
00:14:32,986 --> 00:14:39,986
There must be an amazing world beyond that sky.

198
00:14:39,986 --> 00:14:43,986
Day after day, the moon girl and the forest girl looked at the sky.

199
00:14:43,986 --> 00:14:46,986
I wonder if the forest girl must be her.

200
00:14:47,986 --> 00:14:49,986
Oh, I just don't know.

201
00:14:49,986 --> 00:14:50,986
Hello?

202
00:14:50,986 --> 00:14:52,986
Curry Pie, you're here!

203
00:14:52,986 --> 00:14:54,986
Uh, yep.

204
00:14:55,986 --> 00:14:56,986
Welcome home!

205
00:14:57,986 --> 00:14:58,986
Thanks, Lulu.

206
00:14:59,986 --> 00:15:00,986
Growl!

207
00:15:00,986 --> 00:15:02,986
What book is that?

208
00:15:02,986 --> 00:15:04,986
It's a picture book my mom wrote.

209
00:15:04,986 --> 00:15:05,986
How cool!

210
00:15:05,986 --> 00:15:06,986
May Lulu read it?

211
00:15:06,986 --> 00:15:07,986
Yes, of course.

212
00:15:07,986 --> 00:15:10,986
But I'll warn you, it doesn't have an ending.

213
00:15:10,986 --> 00:15:12,986
Why doesn't it have one?

214
00:15:12,986 --> 00:15:15,986
Because my mom died before she got the chance to finish it.

215
00:15:17,986 --> 00:15:19,986
She was killed by a bear.

216
00:15:20,986 --> 00:15:23,986
Go ahead, I can check on Ginkgo.

217
00:15:23,986 --> 00:15:35,986
Tell me, Ginkgo.

218
00:15:38,986 --> 00:15:41,986
Ginkgo loves you so much! Look at what she's done for you!

219
00:15:42,986 --> 00:15:43,986
Why?

220
00:15:43,986 --> 00:15:45,986
We only just met each other.

221
00:15:46,986 --> 00:15:48,986
And I haven't done anything for you.

222
00:15:48,986 --> 00:15:51,986
Your injuries and your pain should have been mine.

223
00:15:51,986 --> 00:15:54,986
But you sacrificed yourself anyway.

224
00:16:21,986 --> 00:16:27,986
No way she's not done for.

225
00:16:28,986 --> 00:16:30,986
Either way, she'd slow us down.

226
00:16:30,986 --> 00:16:31,986
Let's exclude her.

227
00:16:31,986 --> 00:16:32,986
Exclude her.

228
00:16:32,986 --> 00:16:33,986
Exclude her.

229
00:16:33,986 --> 00:16:34,986
Exclude her.

230
00:16:34,986 --> 00:16:35,986
Exclude her.

231
00:16:35,986 --> 00:16:36,986
Exclude her.

232
00:16:36,986 --> 00:16:37,986
Exclude her.

233
00:16:37,986 --> 00:16:38,986
The animal world is merciless.

234
00:16:38,986 --> 00:16:42,986
The weak, the scared, the ones who can't keep constant within the group.

235
00:16:42,986 --> 00:16:44,986
They are summarily excluded.

236
00:16:44,986 --> 00:16:45,986
Oh no.

237
00:16:45,986 --> 00:16:47,986
It looks like I failed.

238
00:16:47,986 --> 00:16:48,986
Unwanted bear.

239
00:16:48,986 --> 00:16:49,986
You are a lone wolfsbane.

240
00:16:49,986 --> 00:16:50,986
Goodbye.

241
00:16:50,986 --> 00:16:51,986
A lone wolfsbane.

242
00:16:51,986 --> 00:16:52,986
So I don't get to be chosen then.

243
00:16:52,986 --> 00:16:53,986
I don't get to be approved by anyone.

244
00:16:53,986 --> 00:16:54,986
I don't get to be loved.

245
00:16:54,986 --> 00:16:55,986
I'm going to die here without ever being found.

246
00:16:55,986 --> 00:16:56,986
I'm going to die here without ever being found.

247
00:16:56,986 --> 00:16:57,986
This is the love song my mom taught me.

248
00:16:57,986 --> 00:16:58,986
It's okay.

249
00:16:58,986 --> 00:16:59,986
I'm your friend.

250
00:16:59,986 --> 00:17:00,986
You don't have to be alone anymore.

251
00:17:00,986 --> 00:17:01,986
I'm here now and I love you.

252
00:17:01,986 --> 00:17:02,986
Lady, come on.

253
00:17:02,986 --> 00:17:03,986
I don't get to be loved.

254
00:17:03,986 --> 00:17:04,986
I don't get to be loved.

255
00:17:04,986 --> 00:17:07,986
I'm going to die here without ever being found.

256
00:17:07,986 --> 00:17:16,986
This is the love song my mom taught me.

257
00:17:16,986 --> 00:17:18,986
It's okay.

258
00:17:18,986 --> 00:17:20,986
